<title>GERMANY: Hong Kong's Yam - Authority has cut European stake.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong's Yam - Authority has cut European stake.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Joseph Yam, chief executive of the Hong Kong monetary authority, said on Thursday that the body had reduced European exposure in its reserves.</p>
<p>Speaking at a conference on Hong Kong's monetary arrangements through 1997, Yam said. &quot;We have been reducing our exposure to European investments.&quot;</p>
<p>Yam said that 75 percent of Hong Kong's reserves were held in U.S. dollar related investments, so the maximum European exposure was 25 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not know what is going with European currency union. Only after the euro is firmly established can we be sure. In the meantime, if we want to manage risk, we have to reduce our exposure to Europe,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
